Suss numeric conversion helper

The parser and GC integration are original Suss code, licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0.
The helper links ryu-js 1.0.3, a Rust implementation of Ulf Adams' Ryū algorithm
adapted for ECMAScript formatting by the boa-dev project. Upstream repository:
https://github.com/boa-dev/ryu-js (crate registry checksum is in Cargo.lock and
artifact/manifest.json). Copyright 2018 Ulf Adams; Rust port contributors include
David Tolnay and the boa-dev contributors. Upstream Apache-2.0 and Boost Software
License 1.0 texts are retained byte-for-byte in licenses/ryu-js-*.txt.

The compiled helper also links Rust core/compiler support from Rust 1.98.0,
commit 88d9e12ae178fab0fb5cc050a94da85685d449ea. The toolchain's complete
standard-library copyright and license report is retained byte-for-byte as
licenses/Rust-1.98.0-COPYRIGHT-library.html, including its third-party notices.
This report is broader than the code linked into this allocator-free helper;
retaining it does not assert that every listed dependency is linked.
Source: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/tree/88d9e12ae178fab0fb5cc050a94da85685d449ea

Distribute these notices and license files with the numeric Wasm build input and
with distributions containing the generated Suss runtime. No ClojureScript source
was copied into the parser or bridges. The pinned ClojureScript source is a
semantic reference and development oracle, with its original EPL notices intact.
